course: dictionary
lesson: 15473
title: Straightforward: easy or honest
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Straightforward has two meanings. The first is easy to understand or do, with no hidden tricks. «The maths question was straightforward: just add the two numbers.» Nothing tricky was hiding in the question, so it was simple.
explain: The second meaning is about people. A straightforward person is honest and open. «Mia is straightforward, so she told us the truth about the broken vase.» She says what she means and does not hide things.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like easy, clear or honest nearby point to the right meaning. Try swapping in easy or honest: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Straightforward means easy to understand or do, with no hidden difficulties.
fact: «A straightforward recipe» has clear steps that are simple to follow.
fact: A straightforward person is honest and open, and says what they mean.
fact: Teachers may say «This part is straightforward» to calm the class, but «not as straightforward as it looks» means something is harder than it seems.
fact: «Fairly straightforward» means quite easy, and «perfectly straightforward» means completely easy.
exercise: «The directions to the station were straightforward: turn left, then go straight on.» What does straightforward mean here? | Very long and winding | *Easy to follow | Hidden and tricky | Written in a language nobody knows
exercise: «Sam is straightforward, so he always tells us what he really thinks.» What does straightforward suggest about Sam? | Always late for school | *Honest and open | Sneaky and secret | Very tall for his age
exercise: «The quiz was simple, and the answers were clear.» Find and copy one word that means the same as straightforward. | were | quiz | answers | *simple
test: «The instructions on the box were straightforward.» What does straightforward mean? | Missing a page | *Easy to follow | Written in French | Hard to read
test: «Ben is not as straightforward as he looks; he often hides how he really feels.» What does this suggest about Ben? | *He is not fully open | He is always cheerful | He is very good at maths | He is very honest
exam: Which word could replace straightforward in «The puzzle was straightforward»? | *easy | loud | sleepy | heavy
